direction: down
"cursor": "cursor\nResume only operation-qualified current phase; never\nre-enter detached device cleanup or infer kernel\ncompletion from CLOSED"
"wait-context": "wait-context\nRooted cursor, descriptor generation, native pin,\ndesired interest and owner epoch survive wait/GC;\nFDSET borrow ends before dispatch"
"lost-wake": "lost-wake\nArm then recheck durable request/ready state;\nnotification errors need a qualified level-channel\nguarantee; readiness survives interrupt"
"participant": "participant\nReturn from select is not service_sync_op; attach\nroots, join both old members, finish loop/NOOP and\nreload latest epoch"
"unknown": "unknown\nSeparate retryable partial, consumed error and\nunknown native effects; unresolved outcomes retain\nowner and VM custody"
"derived-credit": "derived-credit\nReserve child before escape; lost enqueue keeps\ncredit; independent child may outlive source but\nblocks VM cleanup"
"storage-commit": "storage-commit\nCanonical RC/still/scan/census handoff at complete\nwait-free checkpoint; no live borrowed PSTATE\npointers may migrate"
"vm-permit": "vm-permit\nProcessor exit needs affinity/wait/roster closure;\nVM cleanup additionally requires every\ndescendant/outcome/root/service lease drained"
"cursor" -> "wait-context": "Wait captures exact close cursor"
"unknown" -> "wait-context": "Native outcome controls\nadmissible resume"
"wait-context" -> "lost-wake": "Arm requires pinned complete\ncontext"
"lost-wake" -> "participant": "Wake reaches serviceable old\nowner"
"wait-context" -> "participant": "Roots and borrow release precede\nGC"
"wait-context" -> "storage-commit": "No PSTATE borrow crosses\ntransfer"
"storage-commit" -> "vm-permit": "Storage scanner/census handoff\nacknowledged"
"derived-credit" -> "vm-permit": "All child work accounted and\ndrained for VM"
"unknown" -> "vm-permit": "Unknown native effects block\nretirement"
"participant" -> "vm-permit": "Loop closure and old roster\nreceipt precede exit"
proof: "SysML -> ASCENT -> QNT / Lean; source + platform OPEN"
"vm-permit" -> proof
gain0: "critical-path\nRemoved collective waiting must exceed added critical-\npath coordination; no numeric speedup established"
proof -> gain0
gain1: "resume\nO(1) state per wait; only proven resumable operations\nmay repeat current phase"
proof -> gain1
gain2: "sharing\nReuse only if ownership and sync-op participation\ncontracts coincide; a generic thread pool does not\nsuffice"
proof -> gain2
gain3: "language\nZig cannot remove lifetime, wakeup, affinity or closure\nproof obligations; no mandatory Zig benefit\ndemonstrated"
proof -> gain3
